Android capsule delivery, measured on a Pixel_9a emulator (2026-07-31).

Cause: the crash-path POST races the OS killing the process.

  window between FATAL EXCEPTION and process death   168 ms .. 768 ms
  first HTTP POST on a cold process (to LOCALHOST)    40 ms .. 316 ms

The windows overlap, which is the intermittency. Adding a realistic 2 s
ingest latency makes the loss deterministic: on any real network the
synchronous POST cannot win.

  BEFORE, localhost ingest:      counted=6 capsules=4 nothing=2
  BEFORE, 2 s ingest latency:    counted=2 capsules=0 nothing=2
  AFTER,  2 s ingest latency:    9/9 delivered, 0 lost, 1 skipped

Runs count only when the planted crash is confirmed in logcat, so install
and launch failures are never miscounted as lost capsules.
